1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,795
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:07,340
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,635
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:15,348
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:17,767
[Atoy] <i>If there's another gate there,</i>
<i>it's surely locked too.</i>

6
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:18,768
What will we do?

7
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,979
[Atoy] <i>If there's a lock,</i>
<i>that means there's a key.</i>

8
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,772
[Ibyang] <i>What is your mission?</i>

9
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,065
Let me join!

10
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,567
[Ivan] <i>Is this what you're looking for?</i>

11
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:27,277
We can talk about this.

12
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,237
- [gunshot]
- [groans]

13
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:33,950
PREVIOUSLY

14
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:36,244
[Ame] <i>I told you to stay</i>
<i>with Emerson, right?</i>

15
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:38,872
Let me join, Sister Ame.

16
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:40,206
What exactly are we supposed to do?

17
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:44,627
[Ame] <i>What we need to do is get</i>
<i>Samir's cellphone or wallet.</i>

18
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:46,087
Don't let the captives out!

19
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,589
[gunshots]

20
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:49,299
[shrieks]

21
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,719
[in English] I will kill you.

22
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,179
[grunts]

23
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,346
[in English] Where is my brother?!

24
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,557
[Samir, in English] <i>In hell!</i>
<i>Would you like to say hello?</i>

25
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,768
[grunts and groans]

26
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:02,771
- [Ivan] Don't kill him! We need him alive!
- [gunshots]

27
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,899
[grunts, growls, and groans]

28
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:06,900
- [in English] Only pepper, no spray!
- [pained grunt]

29
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,612
[Artem, in English]
<i>You can do everything you want to him,</i>

30
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:13,323
<i>but your Atoy remains our prisoner.</i>

31
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:15,283
What will we do now?

32
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:17,494
Looks like we're at a dead end.

33
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:18,995
There's another way.

34
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:22,123
[Uno] <i>I'll call our boss to consult him.</i>

35
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:34,093
[suave theme music playing]

36
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:39,349
[music fades]

37
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:43,561
[ominous music playing]

38
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:46,731
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

39
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:49,734
[foreboding music playing]

40
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:54,948
- [music fades]
- [suave theme music playing]

41
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,368
[motorcycle revving]

42
00:01:58,451 --> 00:01:59,327
[sewing machine whirring]

43
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,286
[scratches]

44
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,246
[snipping]

45
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:06,167
[sewing machine clacking]

46
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:08,002
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

47
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:10,421
[gunshots]

48
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:11,840
[clicking]

49
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,258
[snipping]

50
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,309
[music fades]

51
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:25,478
[tense music playing]

52
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:26,813
[phone keypad beeping]

53
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:31,025
[line ringing]

54
00:02:31,109 --> 00:02:31,943
[in English] Bad news.

55
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:33,987
Samir has escaped.

56
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:42,370
[tires screeching]

57
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:49,085
[suspicious music playing]

58
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:52,964
[speaking in Russian] What happened, boss?

59
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:55,550
[in English] I was attacked.

60
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,759
[in English] You're attacked?

61
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:57,969
[in English] Identities?

62
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:00,930
[in English] Friends of Atoy.

63
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:03,850
[in English] I'm glad you're safe, sir.

64
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:07,770
[in English] Anyways, I have news for you.

65
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:10,815
[in English] Our prisoners almost escaped.

66
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:14,110
[in English] Boss, I said almost!

67
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:17,697
[in English] They are back in the cell
and are being punished.

68
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:20,491
- Should we report to the ambassador?
- [In Russian] Never!

69
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,911
[heavy music playing]

70
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:26,581
[in English] We must find his family,
right now.

71
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,084
[in English] Yes, sir.

72
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:35,924
[music swells, fades]

73
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:45,225
[pensive music playing]

74
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:04,118
Audrey, how are you?

75
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,623
I can't sleep.

76
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,502
I don't know anymore

77
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:17,006
how this mess in our lives will end.

78
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,512
I'm restless, Ame.

79
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:27,267
I know I need to be strong, but…

80
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,019
it's hard.

81
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:34,774
But I can't give up now.

82
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:40,655
[melancholic music playing]

83
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,075
We're with you, Audrey.

84
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:47,662
We'll help each other so we can find Atoy.

85
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:50,665
Hmm?

86
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,709
So, how's your foot?

87
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:56,254
It's okay now. I can move it.

88
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:57,964
[Ame chuckles softly]

89
00:04:58,047 --> 00:04:59,882
Oh, by the way.

90
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:02,552
We saw Ibyang earlier.

91
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:04,220
She asked us to give this to you.

92
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:06,431
She said you'll understand it.

93
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:11,728
[sentimental music playing]

94
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:18,359
Oh, sorry. That's probably lukewarm now.

95
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:23,406
You've already done so much for me.

96
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:27,910
You even brought me soft food.
[chuckles softly]

97
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:31,247
I just asked my sisters to buy that.

98
00:05:31,789 --> 00:05:34,292
You even baked for me!

99
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:37,336
- Isn't that harder?
- [laughs]

100
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,380
[chuckles]

101
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:45,595
[sobs and chuckles]

102
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:48,806
Is the taste that bad?

103
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:54,187
This porridge is perfect, Ibyang.

104
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:59,150
[inhales] I was just
wishful thinking that…

105
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:02,153
[sobs] I hope…

106
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:06,157
I hope my child is as kind as you.

107
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:19,045
She remembers you
even if you're far apart,

108
00:06:19,128 --> 00:06:22,173
and even if she's already with her mother.

109
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,554
Ibyang is really sweet, isn't she?

110
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,724
She still remembers me.

111
00:06:32,433 --> 00:06:33,434
[chuckles softly]

112
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:38,815
[gentle music playing]

113
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:40,525
Does she know that

114
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:42,819
her Tatoy is missing?

115
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:46,989
[sighs] We didn't tell her.

116
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:52,495
I don't want to ruin
her bonding with Olga.

117
00:06:53,704 --> 00:06:57,291
This is actually the first time
they're together, just the two of them.

118
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:04,048
Hmm. If I tell her what happened
to Atoy, she'll worry.

119
00:07:05,216 --> 00:07:10,304
[melancholic music playing]

120
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:20,356
Okay. Charmi, we're about to go out now.

121
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,607
Ibyang, come on.

122
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:22,817
Where are we going?

123
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,986
I'll explain it to you later. Huh?

124
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:30,241
[suspicious music playing]

125
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,578
- Uh, good morning, ma'am!
- Oh. Hello, hello.

126
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:35,455
- Uh, ma'am, may I ask something?
- Ah, yes.

127
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:37,415
Where is Olga's house?

128
00:07:39,917 --> 00:07:44,255
Oh, are you the ones my friend said
who would collect the debt?

129
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:46,299
[henchman 1] That's us. She sent us here.

130
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:50,094
Oh, yes! Yes, brother.
Hello. Good morning, brother!

131
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:53,264
She's been waiting for you
since yesterday.

132
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:55,433
- What's--
- Shh.

133
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:58,936
She left last night
because she had a taping.

134
00:07:59,020 --> 00:07:59,979
She'll be gone for three days.

135
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:01,772
Just come back another day.

136
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:03,900
[softly] Just between us.

137
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:08,571
We came from such a far place.
What do we do, miss?

138
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:11,032
Well, what can I do?
You won't be able to get anything.

139
00:08:11,115 --> 00:08:13,659
You won't be able to collect anything.

140
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:15,286
Just come back another day.

141
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:20,166
- Mmm. Okay, okay. All right, we'll leave.
- Okay! Okay.

142
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:21,334
[Charmi] You can pass through there.

143
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:25,421
- [Charmi] All right.
- [phone keypad beeping]

144
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:30,510
[phone ringing]

145
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:31,677
[tense music playing]

146
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:32,637
[Charmi] <i>Friend.</i>

147
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:35,348
You owe me.

148
00:08:35,431 --> 00:08:38,518
There were three men here, collecting.

149
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,229
But you know me.

150
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:44,190
That script of ours is automatic.
I already handled it.

151
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:47,944
What debt? You're unbelievable.
You're putting me and Ibyang in danger!

152
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:50,530
Huh? Why?

153
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:53,533
Those three men you talked to,
they're enemies!

154
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,825
What's wrong with you?

155
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:57,662
Call the police now.
Or-- Or the village police.

156
00:08:57,745 --> 00:08:59,330
<i>Or any of our backup!</i>

157
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:03,292
Oh-- No, no, no. Okay. No, they're gone!

158
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:05,169
- They're still here.
- [gasps]

159
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:07,463
Friend, you're wrong. They're still here!

160
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,758
- There, look!
- [Charmi] <i>Sorry, sorry, sorry!</i>

161
00:09:10,841 --> 00:09:11,759
<i>Sorry, sis!</i>

162
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:14,011
- Friend, I'm sorry. They're still here!
- [indistinct]

163
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:17,890
[gasps] Ibyang! Come, come, come!

164
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:19,517
[panicked gasping]

165
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,562
Here, here, here! Here! [panicked gasping]

166
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:24,146
[in English] Oh my God. [gasping]

167
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:31,237
Come on. [gasping]

168
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:34,490
Wait, wait. Here, here!
Go inside. Get in here, quick!

169
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:37,034
- [music fades]
- [loud sigh]

170
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,122
[in English] I can't reach him again.

171
00:09:42,748 --> 00:09:43,958
He won't answer anymore.

172
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:46,252
Your son decided yesterday.

173
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:48,838
Most likely, he won't talk to us.

174
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:52,675
I just want to know if he's safe,
or where he went!

175
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,176
[mysterious music playing]

176
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:57,096
Where would Audrey go? To Atoy, of course!

177
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:00,391
Do you know where he lives?

178
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:03,227
Not yet, but that's easy.

179
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:05,354
Send our people to Tabang Lupa.

180
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:06,522
Let them observe there.

181
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:08,733
But keep a low profile.

182
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:11,527
[Martina] When you see them,
don't ever hurt my son.

183
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:14,822
And make sure you bring Audrey
and Janine here immediately.

184
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,115
[in English] Okay?

185
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,494
Oh? What are you waiting for? Go!

186
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:21,996
- Let's go!
- Go, go.

187
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:25,124
Anyway,

188
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:29,086
our men who are looking for Olga
and Ibyang have already reported to me.

189
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,632
They're at Olga's house now,
and hopefully by lunchtime,

190
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,467
we'll have Ibyang.

191
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,428
- [suspicious music playing]
- [in English] Finally, some good news.

192
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,974
[music fades]

193
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:43,601
Not here.

194
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:46,020
Check upstairs.

195
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,229
- Come.
- [in English] Yes, boss.

196
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:49,607
[ominous music playing]

197
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,835
[gasps, hushes]

198
00:11:11,962 --> 00:11:13,672
[whispers] Don't make noise.

199
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:19,512
[clattering]

200
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:28,104
[gasping]

201
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:32,441
[suspicious music playing]

202
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:38,656
[henchman 1] What? Are they there?

203
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:39,615
[henchman 2] Not here!

204
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:42,660
Check under their bed! They're just there!

205
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:44,954
They can't escape inside this house!

206
00:11:45,037 --> 00:11:46,122
[henchman 2] All right!

207
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:47,456
[henchman 1] They're just hiding!

208
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:48,666
Open those doors!

209
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:52,002
[rousing music playing]

210
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:53,170
- [spritzing]
- [screaming]

211
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:54,839
Ibyang! Come on, hurry!

212
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:56,090
Come on, come on! Hurry, hurry!

213
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:57,299
[gasps] Ibyang!

214
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:58,592
- [grunts]
- Wait!

215
00:11:58,676 --> 00:11:59,552
What?!

216
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,554
- [grunts] Let me go!
- [rousing music playing]

217
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:05,099
[in English] Dmitri is dead,
and his daughter, Audrey, is missing.

218
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:07,726
[in English] We need
that woman and her daughter!

219
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,687
[in English] Or that man will not talk!

220
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:12,940
[in English] We don't need them
with us to make him talk.

221
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:14,650
[in English] What are you trying to say?

222
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:17,153
[in English] We only need to make
him believe that we have his family.

223
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:19,363
[in English] And how
are we going to do that?

224
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:20,448
[in English] With this.

225
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:23,826
[in English] This was recorded
in the interrogation room

226
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:26,245
after the break-in
at the ambassador's office.

227
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:29,165
[suspicious music playing]

228
00:12:33,461 --> 00:12:35,212
- [device blips]
- [Samir, in English] Start with your name.

229
00:12:40,759 --> 00:12:43,846
[in English] I am Audrey Regalia,

230
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:47,558
the daughter of Dmitri Regalia.

231
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:52,563
[in English] Please tell me what happened
in the ambassador's office.

232
00:12:52,646 --> 00:12:56,692
[in English] Well, the ambassador
was showing us his office

233
00:12:57,318 --> 00:13:00,362
when he noticed
that there was a chair out of place.

234
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:02,114
[in English] When he looked behind it,

235
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,366
he saw there was a hole in the wall.

236
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:06,660
[in English] Window, sorry.

237
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:09,163
[in English] And then, a guy in a mask

238
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:11,332
jumped over the kitchen counter,

239
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:13,667
hit my dad and the ambassador
over the head,

240
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:15,711
and climbed out of the window.

241
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:18,005
[in English] And you do not know this man?

242
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:20,549
[in English] <i>No! He was wearing a mask…</i>

243
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:23,219
[in English] And how is this
supposed to help us?

244
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:25,804
[man, in English] With the help of AI.
We can mimic the woman's voice,

245
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:28,516
and we can make her say anything we want.

246
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:33,395
[in English] Okay. Do it.

247
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:35,523
[in English] Do it now.

248
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:41,695
[music fades]

249
00:13:42,696 --> 00:13:45,115
[grunting and groaning]

250
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:47,660
- [clangs]
- [groans]

251
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,245
[groans]

252
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:52,331
- Ibyang! Come on.
- [henchman groaning]

253
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:54,166
Mama! [squeals]

254
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,876
[gasps]

255
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,922
- [grunting and groaning]
- [squealing]

256
00:14:00,005 --> 00:14:02,049
[gasping]

257
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:03,968
[indistinct chatter]

258
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:07,763
[grunts and groans]

259
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:09,598
You two, out!

260
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,642
- Hurry! Oh!
- Quick, quick, quick!

261
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:15,312
Oh, oh! No one make the wrong move!

262
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,357
Move! Go there! Hurry!

263
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,569
Hurry up! Don't be slow,
and don't you da--

264
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:25,865
Oh! What? One wrong move,

265
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:28,158
I'll put holes in your bodies.

266
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,118
Oh!

267
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:30,995
[scoffs] Oh! Ay! [gasps]

268
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:32,496
[squeals]

269
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,956
[Charmi] I'll report you! Don't--

270
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:36,750
[Charmi grunt, squeals]

271
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:37,668
[Charmi] Friend, run now, friend!

272
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:38,878
The gun is fake.

273
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:42,506
Quick, run now!
We'll hide here! Here, here.

274
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,300
Lie down, lie down, lie down! Duck, duck!

275
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:52,683
[groans]

276
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:54,518
Did you see those three women
who came out?

277
00:14:55,769 --> 00:14:57,438
- [in English] Listen.
- [music fades]

278
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:59,064
[Audrey gasps, in English] <i>Please!</i>

279
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:01,358
[in English] <i>What do you want from us?!</i>

280
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:04,695
<i>Whatever it is, just spare my daughter!</i>

281
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:07,364
<i>Don't take her, please! Have mercy!</i>

282
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:09,742
[in English] What--
What did you do to them?

283
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:12,745
[pensive music playing]

284
00:15:12,828 --> 00:15:14,538
[in English] They are safe.

285
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:18,876
[in English] A little hurt,
but they are safe.

286
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,007
[in English] So now that I have

287
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:29,720
your Audrey and your precious daughter,

288
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:35,935
who will protect them from men like me?

289
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:42,524
[in English] All right! All right.

290
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:48,906
[in English] I'll tell you where it is.

291
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:52,368
[in English] I will tell you
where the laptop is.

292
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:57,706
[in English] Just don't do
anything bad to them.

293
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,417
[in English] You better tell me the truth.

294
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:02,962
[in English] Yes. [sighs]

295
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:09,218
[music fades]

296
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:15,849
They ran there!

297
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:19,395
They said there. Come on!

298
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:20,521
Come on!

299
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:25,359
[somber music playing]

300
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,655
Brother, where are they?

301
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:32,408
Just stay there.
The bastards might come back.

302
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:33,701
Yes, they might come back.

303
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:38,330
[panicked gasping] Friend, it's okay now.

304
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,415
Come on, it's okay now.

305
00:16:39,498 --> 00:16:40,499
- They're gone.
- Okay?

306
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:44,837
[pensive music playing]

307
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:49,466
Friend, we need to leave
because we still have somewhere to go.

308
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:50,968
[panicked breathing]

309
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:53,095
Good thing you arrived.

310
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:56,181
Where are we really going?

311
00:16:57,099 --> 00:17:00,686
We're going to Atoy.
He needs to know something.

312
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:02,062
[Olga] O-Okay, Mars.

313
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:04,398
[stammers] Can you just call him?

314
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:05,858
He's not answering!

315
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:07,151
Go now, leave!

316
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,736
- The two men might come back, hurry!
- Okay, okay.

317
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:10,237
- Come on, quick. Run, run!
- [indistinct]

318
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:13,490
- Quick! Sis, thank you!
- [groans]

319
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:16,326
[music fades]

320
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:21,165
Atoy.

321
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:24,251
They have your wife and child.

322
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:26,628
[suspicious music playing]

323
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:29,840
That means they'll take my child next.

324
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:32,634
Don't worry.

325
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:36,472
They won't hurt you.
You're still useful to them.

326
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:39,308
[sighs]

327
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:41,894
We need to get out of here again.

328
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:49,026
But how? Didn't we already try?

329
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:53,030
We don't even know which hell we're in.

330
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:58,243
[tense music playing]

331
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:01,330
[man 1] <i>Next is the car and the tractor.</i>

332
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:03,916
We're inside a junkyard compound.

333
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:06,293
We need to know the exact location.

334
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:28,774
But there's something
you need to know about Janine.

335
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:31,944
[heavy breathing]
She's not your real child.

336
00:18:32,027 --> 00:18:33,278
[pensive music playing]

337
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:50,003
[knocks on door]

338
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,215
- [Ame] Audrey.
- [door squeaks open]

339
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,135
Um…

340
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:59,346
Do you want some breakfast?

341
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:01,932
No.

342
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:03,976
Thank you.

343
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,563
Are you okay?

344
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:09,773
You look like you didn't sleep.

345
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:16,155
I dreamt of Dad.

346
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:19,950
I found out that

347
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:23,036
he was buried this morning.

348
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,584
I didn't even get to visit him.

349
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,423
It's just sad that…

350
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,385
we ended up like this.

351
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:42,639
[sighs] So toxic.

352
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:51,607
[Ame] Your situation is very pitiful.

353
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,568
I'm sorry.

354
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:59,740
But it's really good you survived
such a chaotic family.

355
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,288
Ame.

356
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:13,295
I don't know what to do anymore.

357
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:19,384
Even this child got dragged in.

358
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:26,266
She'll be even more hurt
when she learns the truth.

359
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:31,021
- [Ame] The truth?
- [pensive music playing]

360
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:39,196
Before we escaped…

361
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,617
my dad told me…

362
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:51,416
Janine is not my real child.

363
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:54,419
- [music intensifies]
- What?

364
00:20:54,503 --> 00:20:55,963
Are you sure?

365
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:57,714
[sniffles]

366
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,802
I don't think he would lie anymore.

367
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:05,764
Ame, let's keep this between us, please.

368
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:09,810
I need to talk to Atoy first.

369
00:21:09,893 --> 00:21:14,773
Then, together we'll tell Janine
the truth.

370
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:21,321
My brother's sin is truly horrible.

371
00:21:22,322 --> 00:21:24,783
So many people got involved,
so many people got hurt.

372
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:27,786
[in English] Dad, those poor girls.

373
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:31,039
Even his own child.

374
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,627
And especially Janine.

375
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:43,927
Did you ask who your real child is?

376
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:47,514
[music fades]

377
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:50,809
I still don't know.

378
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:55,063
[melodramatic music playing]

379
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,065
But wherever she is…

380
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:02,446
I hope I still get to know her.

381
00:22:03,071 --> 00:22:05,532
[music fades]

382
00:22:13,290 --> 00:22:15,417
[epic music playing]

383
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:34,269
<i>The court has released</i>
<i>a warrant of arrest for former</i>

384
00:22:34,352 --> 00:22:35,729
<i>Mayor Rizaldo Coloma,</i>

385
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:38,398
<i>the alleged bagman of corrupt senators…</i>

386
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:40,192
[Emerson] Here we go again.

387
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:41,485
Here's that crocodile again.

388
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:45,781
He never does anything else,
except steal and steal.

389
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:48,575
I'm so furious-- so furious at him.

390
00:22:48,658 --> 00:22:51,078
- I've had enough.
- This is who Atoy should be looking for.

391
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:54,164
<i>…spotted in Vietnam</i>
<i>and still being pursued by authorities.</i>

392
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:56,249
Oh.

393
00:22:57,292 --> 00:22:59,544
Enough of that news.

394
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:01,505
[Cita] We already have
so much to think about,

395
00:23:01,588 --> 00:23:04,257
and that news just ruins the day.

396
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:06,134
This is what
I'm really thinking about, miss.

397
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:09,387
[Emerson] How will they catch
this bastard?

398
00:23:09,471 --> 00:23:10,472
- [Emerson] It won't work again.
- What?

399
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:12,057
- [Emerson] It's not--
- I already turned it off.

400
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,350
[Emerson] The remote isn't working.

401
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:15,727
[Emerson] There are batteries.

402
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:16,770
[Emerson] Oh, that's why.

403
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:18,897
Oh.

404
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:19,898
- Hey. Ibyang!
- Sister Ame!

405
00:23:21,024 --> 00:23:22,984
- Hmm. I missed you.
- [Emerson gasps]

406
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:28,198
[in English] My love, my love.

407
00:23:28,281 --> 00:23:30,033
[soft chuckle]

408
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:31,201
[Emerson, in English] My love.

409
00:23:32,327 --> 00:23:33,245
[happy sigh]

410
00:23:34,454 --> 00:23:38,416
Ame, can you please take Ibyang
to your room first?

411
00:23:39,292 --> 00:23:41,044
Why?

412
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:44,381
- [Cita] Uh…
- [music fades]

413
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:48,426
Uh, Ame, Ibyang's back is wet.
Go on. Change her first, Ame.

414
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:50,262
[Cita] She still has clothes
upstairs, right?

415
00:23:50,345 --> 00:23:51,471
- [Ame] Uh, yes.
- [Cita] Go on.

416
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:53,431
[Emerson] Go on, go on, go on, go on.
Change her now.

417
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:55,308
When she says it, do it right away!

418
00:23:55,392 --> 00:23:57,435
Change her shirt, Ame.
You really should. [huffs]

419
00:23:57,978 --> 00:24:00,355
- Right, my love?
- [sneaky music playing]

420
00:24:00,438 --> 00:24:04,359
Good day. I am Olga.

421
00:24:04,442 --> 00:24:05,527
- Ah, Olga.
- Um…

422
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:08,238
[in English] My future ex-girlfriend.

423
00:24:08,321 --> 00:24:11,658
Uh, Olga, what happened?

424
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:14,327
Why did Ame have to take the child away?

425
00:24:14,411 --> 00:24:15,912
Is there a problem?

426
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:18,957
[sighs] It seems so.

427
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:23,336
[sighs] I've been calling Atoy
for a while.

428
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:24,963
He's not answering.

429
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:28,091
Oh, he hasn't come back yet.

430
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:30,427
Uh, uh…

431
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:33,805
My love, what are you going to tell Atoy?

432
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,516
You can tell me. I'll understand.

433
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:40,979
[rousing music playing]

434
00:24:41,062 --> 00:24:42,564
It's…

435
00:24:44,399 --> 00:24:47,068
Atoy is Ibyang's real father.

436
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:50,614
[tense music playing]

437
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:03,543
[electronic blipping]

438
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:09,591
[Lily, in English] Sir, please.
Have mercy.

439
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:10,508
[grunts]

440
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:12,093
[in English] No, no, no, no!
Stop, stop, stop!

441
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:13,762
[in English] I will give you
what you want!

442
00:25:14,888 --> 00:25:16,640
[in English] I will tell you
where the lap--

443
00:25:16,723 --> 00:25:18,225
[groans]

444
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:19,559
[man, in English] Samir, that's enough.

445
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:22,270
[in English] And what will we do with him?

446
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:25,065
UP NEXT

447
00:25:25,148 --> 00:25:27,943
OMG, Miss C!

448
00:25:29,402 --> 00:25:33,198
Aren't Ibyang and Janine the same age?

449
00:25:33,281 --> 00:25:34,407
[Cita] Oh?

450
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:37,535
Oh, then maybe Ibyang
is also Audrey's child.

451
00:25:37,619 --> 00:25:39,287
Audrey needs to know this.

452
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:41,831
[phone ringing]

453
00:25:42,457 --> 00:25:43,625
Hello?

454
00:25:44,125 --> 00:25:45,335
Ibyang?

455
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:47,963
Ibyang. Ibyang, this is Atoy.

456
00:25:48,546 --> 00:25:49,673
Tatoy?!

457
00:25:50,548 --> 00:25:52,133
[in English] What are you doing?
Who are you talking to?

458
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:54,219
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

459
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:57,555
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

460
00:25:57,639 --> 00:25:59,224
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

461
00:25:59,307 --> 00:26:00,725
‪Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
